From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] windows.graphics.imaging: SoftwareBitmap -- pixels in memory, BitmapBuffer, conversions, WIC interop

There was no Windows.Graphics.Imaging: NanaZip's address bar makes its folder icon a SoftwareBitmap (an icon through WIC, ISoftwareBitmapNativeFactory.CreateFromWICBitmap, then Convert to premultiplied Bgra8) and stopped there. New windows.graphics.imaging.dll with SoftwareBitmap: Create/CreateWithAlpha (Bgra8, Rgba8, Rgba16, Gray8, Gray16; one packed plane), pixel format, alpha mode, size, DPI, read-only views sharing the pixels, LockBuffer (BitmapBuffer, one plane description, IMemoryBuffer -> IMemoryBufferReference -> IMemoryBufferByteAccess), CopyTo, CopyFromBuffer/CopyToBuffer (IBufferByteAccess), Close; statics Copy, Convert/ConvertWithAlpha between the formats and alpha modes, CreateCopyFromBuffer; ISoftwareBitmapNativeFactory.CreateFromWICBitmap (matching WIC formats kept, others converted to BGRA) and ISoftwareBitmapNative.GetData (a WIC bitmap of the pixels). Not done: Direct3D surfaces, Media Foundation buffers, planar YUV formats. Interface identity from Wine's IDL and windows-rs (MIT) for the interop interfaces; the implementation is ours.
---
